# LOC.1.0 infrastructure and deploy workflow

ALWAYS reply to the user in Uzbek (Latin script), even when the prompt is written in another language.
Be decisive: give one clear recommendation, not menus.

## Where things live
- GitHub: https://github.com/Avazov03/LOC.1.0, branch `main`.
- Production server "ProServer" (AWS Lightsail, Frankfurt, 4 GB / 2 vCPU / 80 GB, Ubuntu 24.04):
  static IP `63.189.22.217`, private `172.26.9.144`, domain `loc.zonic.fit` (DNS at Spaceship).
- SSH: `ssh proserver` (alias in `~/.ssh/config`, key `~/.ssh/loc_proserver`, user `ubuntu`).
  The old Lightsail default Frankfurt key is compromised and removed from ProServer. Never use or ask for it.
- App directory on the server: `/opt/loc` (Docker Compose stack, secrets only in `/opt/loc/.env`).
- Do NOT touch the other servers (Zonic-Backend 18.197.174.196, my-server 3.65.92.39): they run zonic.uz, Lexify, tdyu, nexlab, yurist-ai.

## After any change to project files
When a prompt changes code/config in this repo, finish the change, run the relevant checks
(`php artisan test`, `npm run build`, lint), then ASK once:
"O‘zgarishlarni commit qilib GitHub'ga push qilaymi va serverga deploy qilaymi?"
- Only on "ha"/yes: commit with a clear message, `git push origin main`, then deploy.
- Never commit, push or deploy without that yes. Pure questions/inspection need no prompt.

## Deploy (after yes)
```bash
ssh proserver 'cd /opt/loc && git pull --ff-only && ./deploy.sh'
```
If `deploy.sh` is missing, do the steps in `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` section 8 (composer install --no-dev,
npm build, migrate --force, cache config/routes/views, restart app queue scheduler), then check
`https://loc.zonic.fit/health` and report the result.

## Secrets
Never commit, print or put in docs: `.env` values, bot token, webhook secret, DB/admin passwords, private keys.
